  message: "In this playbook, \"(Motivating incident: session_retrospective_04262026_1911.md Finding 6 — the agent filed a fresh INV item for what turned out to be...\"\n\nshould instead read\n\n\"(We discovered these failure modes when the agent filed a fresh INV item for what turned out to be...\"\n\n\nAlso: does `scripts/tracker` have a way to enumerate all tags? If not, we should make a WI for that and make that WI block the present one (which I am re-opening)."  # 7a25
- op: discuss  # 49aa
  at: '2026-04-27T14:31:28Z'  # 49aa
  by: agent  # 49aa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 49aa
  clock: 7  # 49aa
  nonce: 49aa  # 49aa
  message: "Confirmed and re-opened. Two follow-up actions taken in this turn:\n\n(1) Verified `scripts/tracker` has no tag-enumeration command. The subcommand list — show/list/ready/log/add/update/discuss/lock/unlock/freeze/unfreeze/repair-drift/promote/demote/stealth/unstealth/delete/validate/count-todos/hash-todos/guidance/check-messages/init/setup/cache-rebuild/reconcile-reset/fork-setup/migrate/sync/tui/serve/deps/batch — has nothing for it; `list --tag` filters by an already-known value but cannot enumerate; `batch` is unrelated. So the playbook's 'spot-check titles' step at point 1 ('run scripts/tracker list --tag <plausible-tag>') currently relies on the agent guessing tag names from memory.\n\n(2) Filed WI-lifal-tadah-nabup-soriv-sofan-tomiz-sagor-jimaz (P3, todo_soft) and added an isbefore edge from it to WI-mobup, so WI-lifal blocks resumption of WI-mobup per your directive. Status of WI-mobup left at todo_soft (it was already there); flipping it to a more blocked-looking state would be redundant since the isbefore edge already encodes the dependency.\n\n(3) On the wording fix ('Motivating incident: …' → 'We discovered these failure modes when …'): I have NOT applied it yet. Two paths:\n\n  (a) Land it as a small standalone PR right now while WI-mobup awaits WI-lifal — pure prose change, 1 line, doesn't touch the call-site that needs tag enumeration.\n  (b) Hold it inside the resumed WI-mobup PR after WI-lifal lands — keeps the WI-mobup branch a single coherent diff.\n\nI lean (a) since the wording change is independent of tag enumeration and waiting on it leaves stale text in the file that's already injected into agents' context every session. But your call. Awaiting your direction."  # 49aa
